================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SecretRotationPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success plus
the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable SecretRotationDataSource seam whose value types
mirror the KMP OperatorConfidence SecretRotationResponse/SecretRotationStatus 1:1 (production binds
OperatorConfidenceStore.secretRotation() through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the overdue-rotations (critical>0) AlertBanner,
the four severity StatCards (Tracked secrets / OK / Warn / Critical, shown only when items>0), and the
rotation-status GlassPanel with an adaptive table — a columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-secret cards on
iPhone — covering all six web columns (Kind+target, Last rotated+relative, Age, Expires+days-remaining,
Warn/critical thresholds, severity badge) using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass).
Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (21 keys); display
formatting (fmtNumber/plainNumber/dateTime/relative) is ported and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by
isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed model harness (30/30). The full
xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to pre-existing, out-of-scope breakage in TeslaSync/shared-surfaces +
TeslaSync/feature-views (PROVEN by a pristine-tree rebuild that fails identically with zero of my files
